laurel mu 0104 (DarwinBoot, external/UniXNU/drivers/DarwinBoot): the kernel also owns UEFI's own boot-time memory right above the window.
UEFI allocates top-down from the end of "Kernel RAM" (mu 0101), so its loaded images, pool pages, page tables and DarwinBoot's own image sit
in the 176 MiB above the 3904 MiB window the ADT asks for (mkadt.py --dram auto leaves that room). After ExitBootServices every page of type
EfiLoaderCode/Data, EfiBootServicesCode/Data and EfiConventionalMemory is free (UEFI 2.10, 7.2), and DarwinEnter turns the MMU off before the
branch, so nothing of the firmware runs or is read after it. New DarwinBootPkg/Driver/WindowTop.h: DarwinWindowTop walks the final memory map
(the one ExitBootServices takes) from the window end over such descriptors contiguous with it, stops at runtime-services, reserved, ACPI, MMIO,
persistent or EFI_MEMORY_RUNTIME memory, and returns a 2 MiB multiple, at most DARWINBOOT_MAX_WINDOW - window. boot_args memSize =
memSizeActual = window + top; the owned range of DarwinEnter's cache clean grows by it. Screen line "WINDOW +<bytes> UEFI TOP" (row 1), log
line "DARWINBOOT: window top: +0x.. bytes ...". XNU (laurel 3022) says "LAUREL RAM: on: 4078 MiB ...; +174 MiB above the 3904 MiB the ADT
asks: UEFI's boot memory, given by DarwinBoot" and runs its 2100/2974 checks on the whole size. Kill switch: "laurelramtop=0" in the command
line (DarwinBoot reads it; no rebuild). Host test: scripts/laurel/test-darwinboot-top.sh (tools/darwinboot-top-test on the header of this patch).
Not taken, by design: 0x65E00000-0x7CC00000 (366 MiB free in bank A) and the UEFI heap/FD at 0x5FC00000-0x65D00000: not contiguous with the
window, and XNU manages one physical range. docs/laurel_sprout/clocks-on-motion.md "RAM".
